  "body": "The Western Hotel and Wolf Point covered wagons now have deeper canvas drape between their bows. Both retain their existing distinct finishes, weathering, gear, positions and bearings. The new 20\u201328 mm drape is reconstructed; it is not a measured historic textile construction.\n\nThis is a bounded improvement under T-2980. Photographic materials and finishing, distinct compressed LODs, complete current scene rendering, occupants and interaction remain open. T-2980 must not close automatically when this increment merges.\n\nValidation on commit `0656467069ee3f8d0a40685ee571ceaaf4b0a2d7`, tree `6593357c4e0f98003ff3169392ce4ca5be4b6e9a`:\n\n- Full normal preflight passed: 1,046 checks, including 381 self-tests, with the tested tree unchanged.\n- Actual committed-HEAD changelog and ID checks passed, followed by postcommit publication and exact mirror checks.\n- Production regeneration matches both variants and all seven products; covered identity, chart refusal and placement checks passed.\n\nCurrent published desktop/mobile qualification is pending; this PR remains draft. Earlier mobile evidence includes a deadline failure followed by a separate two-image continuation, and does not constitute a whole-gate pass. An earlier preflight was aborted after a ticket-bootstrap clone exhausted storage; its failure is retained separately from the later successful normal run. No assertion was weakened.\n\nDEV only. Recovery source, prior failures and handover are pushed in `kevinrhaas/chicago-tickets`.\n",
